win32u: Set up the user lock and the hardware profile key on first use.

Some of Creative Cloud 6.11's self-update helpers (AdobeIPCBroker.exe, ADSCustomHook.exe) reach
win32u before user32 has initialized it: user_mutex was still uninitialized, so the first
NtUserCreateWindowEx (an HWND_MESSAGE window) hung on a futex, and config_key was still NULL, so
the display config couldn't be read. Initialize the mutex with pthread_once from user_lock and
open the hardware profile key lazily. With this ADSCustomHook finishes ("Successfully executed").

--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -50,6 +50,16 @@
 static const char config_keyA[] = "\\Registry\\Machine\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Hardware Profiles\\Current";
 static const char directx_keyA[] = "\\Registry\\Machine\\Software\\Microsoft\\DirectX";
 
+/* the hardware profile key, opened on first use: processes that reach the display code before
+ * user32 initializes (sysparams_init) need it too; a process with a restricted token can't create
+ * keys under HKLM, it can still read them */
+static HKEY hw_profile_key(void)
+{
+    if (!config_key && !(config_key = reg_create_ascii_key( NULL, config_keyA, 0, NULL )))
+        config_key = reg_open_ascii_key( NULL, config_keyA );
+    return config_key;
+}
+
 static const char devpropkey_gpu_uuidA[] = "Properties\\{233A9EF3-AFC4-4ABD-B564-C32F21F1535C}\\0002";
 static const char devpropkey_gpu_luidA[] = "Properties\\{60B193CB-5276-4D0F-96FC-F173ABAD3EC6}\\0002";
 static const char devpkey_device_driver_date[] = "Properties\\{A8B865DD-2E3D-4094-AD97-E593A70C75D6}\\0002";
@@ -301,6 +311,7 @@
